# INPUT assets for make_media.py. assets/ itself IS tracked (it holds sparusII.png, the
# 48 KB AUV sprite): the whole point of assets/ is that these are inputs, not products,
# so a `rm -rf results/` must not take them with it.
# The stereo photomosaics are the exception — 178 MB of PNG has no business in git. They
# stay out of the repo but out of results/ too, so they survive a results/ wipe. Both
# consumers already degrade gracefully without them (fig_layer_stack falls back to an
# empty frame, fig_octagon_vs_lawnmower skips with a message).
assets/mosaics/
